{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405158-new-procedures-for-technocrats-subliminal-messages","id":1405158,"title":"New Procedures for Technocrats - Subliminal Messages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-29T08:07:03-07:00","id":1405158,"title":"New Procedures for Technocrats - Subliminal Messages","content":"\u200bI thought up some new Procedures for Technocrats of the New World Order. Subliminal messaging is one of the most common urban legends. I've taken it to the logical extreme in WoD. Criticism and new ideas are welcome!<br /> <br /> In the XX and the ongoing XXI centuries, the Technocracy managed to reach heights of Enlightened Science that cemented their position. The New World Order has seeded subliminal messages (combinations of text, signs, and images) in the media commonly used by the Masses - the television, radio, and the parts of the internet containing mass media. This makes mundane humans (and even Acolytes and Consors of Mystick Mages) vulnerable to Procedures developed by the NWO. Through studying the subliminal messages, the Technocrats of the NWO can choose just the right combination of words, tone, circumstances, and body language to trigger responses seeded in the minds of the targets.<br /> Some Tradition Mages who are aware of this have commented that these Subliminal Messages are virtually identical to a Mystickal Technognostic code.<br /> <br /> These Procedures can be used against any mundane humans who have been exposed to television, radio, and some parts of the internet. Just a few weeks of exposure is enough for a person to be susceptible for years.<br /> These Procedures cannot be used against Nightfolk - Mages, Vampires, Garou, and others - for they have concerns that are wholly unlike the blunt simplicity employed in the Subliminal Code. Acolyte, Ghouls or Kinfolk are still susceptible, though at Storyteller's discretion they might be so removed from the contemporary mass culture that the Subliminal Message will make no impression on them. Technocrats are also not susceptible to the Subliminal Message.<br /> <br /> Mind 2: Subliminal Message - Hesitation<br /> <i>&quot;Is this new offer or product good, and will it make me happier? Just how good this primary school is for my children? Is the car I spent my savings on worth it?&quot;</i><br /> This seemingly humble Procedure has a multitude of uses. Inspiring hesitation in a person can make them more likely to accede to demands of the Technocracy's agents. At the very least, it buys extra time, and thus an opportunity to deliver further arguments. At best, it can be used to undermine a person's opinions and values, and make them doubt the very basics of their day-to-day life.<br /> <br /> Mind 3: Subliminal Message - Fear<br /> <i>&quot;Will my job stay as good as it seems now? Is my husband cheating on me, and with who? Are my children safe in this new neighborhood?&quot; </i><br /> Fear is perhaps the emotion to which the least of the Masses would admit to. As such, they are unprepared to deal with it directly when a Technocrat inspires it in them. Fear can directly undermine the present actions of the person, and make them give the Technocrat the respect she or he deserves.<br /> <br /> Mind 4: Subliminal Message - Paranoia<br /> <i>&quot;Did the man who just walked by was a junkie, or maybe even a drug dealer? Is my boss looking for a way to lay me off at first opportunity? Is my family plotting against me?&quot;</i><br /> A person who experiences this Subliminal Message is prepared to do a lot (or give up a lot) to be given a solution to their seeming problems. They will also act distinctly unlike themselves, while at the same time abandoning the values that hold them close to others.<br /> <br /> Mind 5: Subliminal Message - Subservience<br /> <i>&quot;It seems I never amounted to much - I wish I could act towards a constructive goal. At the last family meeting I couldn't even name my achievements. I envy persons who work towards a higher ideal.&quot;</i><br /> While difficult to execute, even partial success of Subservience will result in a person keenly responding to the dictates and orders of a Technocrat. Given minimal prodding - whether threats or an incentive - the person will seek to act under the direction of a Technocrat to the best of their ability. They will eagerly seek encouragement and will modify their outlook and values according to what the Technocrat states.<br /> <br /> Mind 1: Detect Subliminal Imprint<br /> While the vast majority of the Masses are susceptible to the Subliminal Code, there are notable exceptions. Subsistence farmers, very old persons, sheltered children, traditional communities - all of these have not been exposed to enough of the Subliminal Code to be susceptible to these Procedures. Other possible exceptions are Acolytes of Mages, Ghouls, or Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> To be able to act with certainty, this Procedure has been developed. The Technocrat places a small device on the level of eyesight of a person. This device projects an intense Subliminal Message and scans the target's retinas for recognition. If the target subconsciously recognizes the Subliminal Code, then it is a certainty that they are susceptible to the above Procedures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-29-2020, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:26:00-07:00","id":1405162,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s nice, I imagine my virtual adept also having subliminals, he like intersected a Pentex shipment of electronics, and hacked in anti-O'Tolley's and other Pemex subsides messages, hey hope to have it get discovered and have the Pentex divisions go to war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:38:13-07:00","id":1405167,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that modern NWO agents are more interested in the likes of Memetics, which subsumes Subliminal Programming. <br /> <br /> I also tend to think that the Effects you're describing would all require the same level of Mind; what would distinguish them would be what kinds of Feats they count as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T11:45:44-07:00","id":1405185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405158-new-procedures-for-technocrats-subliminal-messages?p=1405167#post1405167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also tend to think that the Effects you're describing would all require the same level of Mind; what would distinguish them would be what kinds of Feats they count as.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, I have thought about this. It makes more sense to me for it to be in the Mind 2 ---&gt; Mind 5 progression. It is written in M20 Mind Magick write-up that<br /> Mind 4 - Control Conscious Mind / Alter Consciousness &quot;<i>The fearsome power of Black Suits and psychic assailants allows the mage to command another person\u2019s actions as well as her thoughts, alter her perceptions or mental state (...) At this Rank, a mage can change someone\u2019s memories, drive her crazy (or sane) (...)</i>&quot;<br /> Mind 5 - Control Subconsciousness &quot;<i>He may alter someone\u2019s mind forever, raising (or lowering) her Traits, rewriting her personality, changing her Nature Trait (...)</i>&quot;<br /> To give a sense of progression, I placed the Fear Procedure at Mind 3, though I could easily see it being Mind 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-29-2020, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}